<figure id="A1.F59.fig3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center">
<p id="A1.F59.fig3.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="A1.F59.fig3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle" style="--ltx-border-color:#000000;padding:0.0pt;"><img src="2509.20328v1/figures-compressed/arc-agi_res_arc-agi-1a_frame191.jpg" id="A1.F59.g3" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/268;" width="476" height="268" alt="Refer to caption"></span></p>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A1.F59.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 59</span>: </span><span id="A1.F59.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Rule extrapolation<span id="A1.F59.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> inspired by ARC-AGI <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>]</cite>. Prompt: <span id="A1.F59.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">“Modify the lower-right grid to adhere to the rule established by the other grids. You can fill cells, clear cells, or change a cell’s color. Only modify the lower-right grid, don’t modify any of the other grids. Static scene, no zoom, no pan, no dolly.”</span> Success rate: 0.08. While Veo 3 doesn’t follow the prompt perfectly, the output grid (bottom right) is completed correctly.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Quantitative results: experimental details</h2>

<figure id="A2.T1" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A2.T1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 1</span>: </span><span id="A2.T1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Video count breakdown for quantitative tasks<span id="A2.T1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">. For segmentation, <math id="A2.T1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\times 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\times 1</annotation></semantics></math> splits indicate one test set with two different background color prompts (white/green). For the prompt sensitivity study on the symmetry task (<a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Prompting best practices ‣ Video models are zero-shot learners and reasoners" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">App.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a>), <math id="A2.T1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\times 10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\times 10</annotation></semantics></math> splits indicate 2 splits (random/shape) across 10 tested prompt variations. For the qualitative tasks, we additionally generated 744 videos (62 tasks <math id="A2.T1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> 12 samples).</span></span></figcaption>
