<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A4.F62.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 62</span>: </span><span id="A4.F62.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Monocular depth estimation<span id="A4.F62.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">. Prompt: <span id="A4.F62.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">“The image transitions to a depth-map of the scene: Darker colors represent pixels further from the camera, lighter colors represent pixels closer to the camera. The exact color map to use is provided on the right side of the image. Static scene, no pan, no zoom, no dolly.”</span> Failure: Veo 3 seems generally unable to color pixels by depth beyond a binary foreground/background mapping and specifically struggles with using a provided color map.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
