<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A4.F63.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 63</span>: </span><span id="A4.F63.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Monocular surface normal estimation<span id="A4.F63.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">. Prompt: <span id="A4.F63.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">“The image transitions to a surface-normal map of the scene: the red/green/blue color channel specify the direction of the surface-normal at each point, as illustrated on the right side of the image on a sphere. Static scene, no pan, no zoom, no dolly.”</span> Failure: While Veo 3 shows some promise in coloring surfaces according to their orientation (e.g., the cube in the front), coloration is inconsistent (compare the two cubes) and doesn’t correctly interpolate colors (e.g., for the slope on the triangle).</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
