<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A4.F77.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 77</span>: </span><span id="A4.F77.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Motion planning<span id="A4.F77.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">; an instance of the piano mover’s problem. Prompt: <span id="A4.F77.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">“The red couch slides from the left room over into the right room, skillfully maneuvering to fit through the doorways without bumping into the walls. The walls are fixed: they don’t shift or disappear, and no new walls are introduced. Static camera, no pan, no zoom, no dolly.”</span> Failure: violating rigid-body integrity, not keeping to permissible transformations (rotation, translation).</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>LLM use.</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Gemini 2.5 Flash and Gemini 2.5 Pro  <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>]</cite> were used for brainstorming task ideas, suggesting related work that we might have otherwise missed, coding support, and to polish human writing.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Image sources.</h2>

