ers and reasoners" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36</span></a>, <a href="#A1.F13" title="Figure 13 ‣ A.1 Perception ‣ Appendix A Qualitative results:Perception, Modeling, Manipulation, Reasoning ‣ Video models are zero-shot learners and reasoners" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>, <a href="#A1.F14" title="Figure 14 ‣ A.1 Perception ‣ Appendix A Qualitative results:Perception, Modeling, Manipulation, Reasoning ‣ Video models are zero-shot learners and reasoners" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>, <a href="#A1.F15" title="Figure 15 ‣ A.1 Perception ‣ Appendix A Qualitative results:Perception, Modeling, Manipulation, Reasoning ‣ Video models are zero-shot learners and reasoners" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>, <a href="#A1.F38" title="Figure 38 ‣ A.3 Manipulation ‣ Appendix A Qualitative results:Perception, Modeling, Manipulation, Reasoning ‣ Video models are zero-shot learners and reasoners" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">38</span></a>, <a href="#A1.F37" title="Figure 37 ‣ A.3 Manipulation ‣ Appendix A Qualitative results:Perception, Modeling, Manipulation, Reasoning ‣ Video models are zero-shot learners and reasoners" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">37</span></a> and <a href="#A4.F74" title="Figure 74 ‣ Appendix D Failure cases ‣ Video models are zero-shot learners and reasoners" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">74</span></a>: The original macaw image was generated with Gemini and, depending on the figure, subsequently modified by the authors (e.g., conversion to grayscale, adding noise, adding the monkey with Nano Banana).</p>
